# Configure and Run Vonage Video API Reference App for React

## What is Vera?

The **Vonage Video API Reference App for React** (Vera) is an open-source video conferencing application built with the [Vonage Video API](https://developer.vonage.com/en/video/client-sdks/web/overview) and the React framework.

It demonstrates best practices for integrating the Vonage Video API into a production-grade application and comes with a rich set of features out of the box:

- Landing page to create and join meeting rooms
- Waiting room with audio/video device preview
- Video conferencing room supporting up to 25 participants
- Screen sharing, group chat, and emoji reactions
- Composed archiving (meeting recording)
- Live captions
- Background blur and virtual background effects
- Active-speaker detection and dynamic layout management

## What you will learn

By the end of this tutorial you will be able to:

1. **Create a Vonage application** in the developer dashboard and obtain the credentials needed to power the Video API.
2. **Configure the backend** by supplying your `VONAGE_APP_ID` and `VONAGE_PRIVATE_KEY` to the environment file.
3. **Install dependencies** using Yarn.
4. **Start the app** in development mode and access it in the browser.

## Project architecture

Vera is a monorepo managed by [Nx](https://nx.dev). The two main workspaces are:

| Workspace | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `frontend` | React + Vite application served on port **5173** in development |
| `backend`  | Express API server served on port **3345** |

The backend generates Vonage Video API session tokens and manages session lifecycle. The frontend connects to those sessions and renders the video conferencing UI.

## Prerequisites

Make sure the following tools are installed on your machine before continuing:

- **Node.js 22** – [Download](https://nodejs.org/en/download/releases/)
- **Yarn** – [Install instructions](https://yarnpkg.com/getting-started/install)
- A **Vonage API account** – [Sign up for free](https://dashboard.vonage.com/?utm_source=DEV_REL&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=vonage-video-react-app)

> **Tip:** Use [nvm](https://github.com/nvm-sh/nvm) to manage Node.js versions. A `.nvmrc` file is included in the repository — run `nvm use` from the project root to switch to the correct version automatically.

---

In the next step you will create a Vonage application and download the private key that the backend needs to authenticate with the Video API.
